DevSupport report: `ASOBO_GT_Update` / `Asobo_Update_Template` on a Landmark SimObject did not run — an L:var it was meant to write stayed `0` (checked in DevMode Behaviors tool). Verified fix: drive the object from a WorldScript `SimMission.Calculator` that computes and writes `L:` vars, consumed by `animations.xml` / `soundai.xml`. Example (resolved thread):

(E:TIME OF DAY, Enum) 2 <= (A:AMBIENT PRECIP STATE, mask) 2 ==
and d (L:ESD_DawnDuskNoWX) != if{ (>L:ESD_DawnDuskNoWX) }
